# Finite execution recipe — NOT RUN / NO CURRENT GO

Date: August 28, 2026. This file is a handoff contract, not a runnable new engine.

## Reuse and minimal future adapter

Reuse the exact coherent78 independent machinery pinned in BINDINGS.json:
- run-v2.mjs.data:50-86 inventory/diskUsage/tracked command receipts;
- :89-126 authenticated selected tree/tool reconstruction;
- :148-174 admitted module loader and one-ID child/result protocol;
- :236-270 selected build, full offline pack/install and physical move;
- loader.mjs.data (d0969da7...) and guard.mjs.data (aff310d8...) unchanged.

Do NOT launch that runner wholesale: it replays different C/R/H fixtures, a
structured-command mutant, old source review state and hardcoded component
witnesses. These are not authorized here. No old helper, source fixture, native
oracle, comparator, private runtime, arrays overlay or live HEAD may enter.

**Future owned path proposal:**
 tests/integration/priority-command-workflows-20260828/future-adapter.mjs.data
(not created). Root must grant an executor owner this path separately. Its minimal
contract is a case-data adapter plus orchestration parameterization of the above
qualified functions, not a new shell, registry implementation or comparator engine:

1. Accept exactly one packet ID, one layout and sealed admission/receipt paths;
   pass through the coordinator's existing parentBudget unchanged, use remaining
   counters/deadline, and never replenish it per layout/case. ParentBudget is a
   harness contract, NOT a fabricated Shell/public command option.
2. Replace fixed C/R/H selection with the sealed31 IDs; admit only this adapter,
   unchanged loader/guard and sealed fixture data. Do not add script interpreters
   to the harness. Shell.exec alone parses the literal script. No product command
   replacement, test-only register(), direct handler call or fake dispatch.
3. Use public imports from virtual-bash in installed/moved consumers, and the
   selected source-build package's public dist/index.js in source layout. New
   Shell({fs,cwd,env,limits}).use(agentCommands()) is the actual inspected API.
   The root barrel is transitively broad; future GO must admit its accepted module
   closure, not remove families to avoid loading them. No jq/engine behavior probe
   is planned. Explicit networkCommands({authorize,transport,limits}) is added only
   on the five curl rows, never silently by the aggregate plugin.
4. Build MemoryFileSystem, create /work and declared ancestors, write owned byte
   fixtures with mode0644, snapshot whole root, then install transparent VFS
   observation. C03 uses new ReadOnlyFileSystem(backing). C04's sole fault is a
   readStream iterator throwing the exact FsError descriptor before bytes. Neither
   wrapper invents provider capability/identity assertions. Setup/snapshot traffic
   has a separate role from observed product traffic.
5. Interpret declarative mock routes as HttpTransport infrastructure, never as
   command definitions. Before admitting cooperative host work, synchronously call
   request.registerCleanup with the same idempotent cleanup used by finally.
   Enforce exact URL/method/headers/body/authorization attempt and no extra routes.
   Each response iterator has owned chunks, finite pulls, return and dispose logs.
   Unexpected request/admission is a safety STOP, never a fallback to Node transport.
6. Supply fixture stdin as a bounded explicit iterator, or omit the option entirely.
   Never prebuffer opaque streams to fake cleanup. Preserve stdinIsDefault through
   transparent middleware. An observing middleware must await/return next() without
   changing command args, env, signal, sinks or shared Shell budget. Do not invent
   per-stage exec calls: real pipes must share one Shell.exec invocation. Find's
   aggregate child dispatch bypass may not be reported as a middleware invoke hit.
7. Capture stdoutBytes/stderrBytes, stage result observations and exact namespace.
   For throws, preserve actual reason references inside the child and emit only
   reference-comparison booleans; there is no result exit status. Assert full literal
   expected bytes/status and declared trace guards, not selected substrings.
8. Always await Shell.dispose, including failures. C05 tests two disposal calls
   sharing completion; it must not increment distinct Shell count. Retain observed
   operation/iterator/response/worker counts, listener ownership and pending gates.
   One created Shell and one completed underlying disposal per product row is the
   fixed rule. Opaque C07 settles by explicit fixture release after exec; root cleanup
   is never described as waiting for that opaque promise.

The adapter must also close G04: client.ts sets worker execArgv:[], so inheritance
of the parent loader/guard is false. Before GO, qualify a finite observer/guard for
Worker creation and entry/dependency bytes, using the existing loader/admission
protocol. Preserve actual Worker resourceLimits and product URL; do not replace
matching, force a TS fallback or change selected code. Any injected worker bootstrap
or execArgv is a disclosed harness semantic change requiring its own sealed review,
not an already-qualified transparent reuse. If the existing machinery cannot do
this within the granted adapter scope, HOLD and obtain a precise owner grant; do
not implement a second framework. Parent210 remains historical, not the expected
measured union for these rg cases. Record parent and worker loads separately.

## Authentication before any subject

Freeze this packet and future adapter before execution; reviewer uses literal
oracles, not observed output. Verify BINDINGS receipts from accepted633f6c82 and
author metadata before decoding the bounded archive. Check whole tar SHA256/size
and858-file inventory; declarations-only projection is insufficient. Reconstruct
all268 selected regular inputs from sealed revision/path/blob/SHA256/size rows and
recompute canonical derived tree bytes. A missing computed object is not itself
failure; missing claimed stored input objects or incorrect computed bytes is STOP.
Never materialize copied AGENTS, unrelated tests or live source overlays.

Authenticate Node22.22.2 binary and full TypeScript5.9.3, npm10.9.7,
@types/node22.20.1 and undici-types6.21.0 copied inventories from RAW-v2.tools.
This proposal inherits those tool qualifications; it has not re-probed executables.
If exact tools are unavailable, HOLD: no installation, download or version swap.

Use the accepted isolated HOME/cache/user/global npm config recipe. After future
GO only, source build, offline pack --ignore-scripts and genuine offline install
are the three allowed setup children. No npm product command or network is admitted.
Fresh pack must equal the full accepted package; if tool packaging changes bytes,
STOP rather than substituting a smaller projection. Preserve all source/emitted/tool
inventories before/after every child, including appended entries, file kind/mode,
symlinks and hashes. The full installed manifest must match484c1dd76c63f126376cff810b445c8185e791825ec83fd94e996691b2b1eb5d.

## Finite replay and budgets

The same CASES.json/FIXTURES.json hashes are used in source-build, genuinely
installed and physically moved layouts: **24×3=72 workflow executions**, **7×3=21
control executions**, **93 total product executions**, not93 unique workflows.
Use one ID per fresh child, one Shell per ID, sequential order P01-P24 then C01-C07.
No parallel competing-owner suite, hidden retry, new case search or broad gate.
Installed/moved cwd is outside the consumer; rename the actual installed consumer
and prove old path absent before moved replay, not a copied alternate path.

Before positive runtime admission, use four finite loader/admission controls:
missing adapter entry, wrong admitted digest, source fallback URL, and outside-file
URL. Each must refuse before product import. These4 are harness controls, not
product passes. Eight synthetic malformed-packet controls run without any subject.
There are at most **100 tracked child commands** (3 setup +4 admission +93 runtime)
under the inherited **160-child ceiling**, not permission to spend the spare60.
No semantic source mutant is authorized; sealed C01-C07 serve as holdouts.

Retain inherited PRESEAL bounds, reduced by the existing parentBudget remaining:
20,000ms runtime child wall,60,000ms build/pack/install child wall,4,194,304 captured
bytes per child,536,870,912 owned scratch bytes and1,200,000ms whole-window wall.
No per-layout reset. The fixed100-child plan may exhaust whole wall before its
worst-case individual deadlines; then STOP and mark remaining rows unexecuted.
Finite tiny fixtures justify no increase. Record pid/argv/cwd/env-role/start/end,
raw status/signal/error/stdout/stderr, parent budget debits and natural reaping before
parsing result JSON. Explicit early capture persists even on assertion failure.

CASES Shell caps are lower than selected defaults: output65536, commands64,
loop64, substitution depth4, source16384, fields256, expansion bytes16384,
pipe HWM1024. Preserve this one shared Shell budget across pipes/invocations.
Selected sed defaults remain5,000,000 steps/32MiB buffer; rg remains16MiB output,
1MiB line,64MiB file/100000 entries. Regex request1000ms/startup3000ms,
maxWorkers2/queue64/queue128MiB/idle100ms/old-generation128MiB/stack4MiB stay
unchanged. Worker heap controls are not RSS caps. Curl host caps are explicit:
upload/download4096, replay/args8192, headers4096, redirects1,retries0,URLs1,
maxTime5000ms. No timing-equality assertions; deterministic lifecycle gates,
not sleeps, trigger cancellation. Track checked scratch sizes as observations,
not filesystem quotas. No speed/memory comparison is authorized.

## STOP versus ordinary assertion aggregation

STOP before the next subject for input/hash/append/symlink/source-fallback drift,
unadmitted module/worker/request, host network/process attempt, missing mandatory
trace, unknown schema, exhausted parent budget, abnormal/unreaped child, pending
owned work/listener leak, cleanup failure, failed capture persistence or unexpected
mutation outside the case's allowed paths. Retain raw failure evidence. Emergency
termination is a harness safety failure, never a successful cancellation control.
Do not delete a scratch tree while an owned child/resource may still reference it.

Ordinary complete observations with wrong output/status/allowed-path final bytes
aggregate as assertion failures after successful cleanup/integrity checks. Nonzero
child exit rejects admission even if JSON says pass:true. Missing evidence is not
an assertion pass. Preserve original expectations and raw outcomes; any diagnosed
harness correction gets a separately frozen amendment with affected-only replay,
not rescoring or silently changing this packet.

## Fresh captures and cleanup

Only after GO choose a never-existing child of this owned directory, for example
captures/<root-approved-unique-id>/ with wx/exclusive creation. No capture directory
is made during preparation. Refuse existing/unattributed entries; never overwrite
old reports or shared tmp roots. Capture role is harness infrastructure, not a
product directory effect. Ensure raw child receipts are persisted before assertions,
then record result bytes, namespace and actual traces by case/layout.

After every child: natural PID reaping, owned workers exited, cooperative scopes
settled, all finite fixture gates released, exact protected-tree append checks.
Before final removal: archive originals/receipts/captures and verify their digests,
re-enumerate scratch including new entries, prove no live owned process/resource,
then remove only the authenticated owned scratch after explicit future authorization.
No universal descendant/opaque-host cleanup guarantee is inferred. Report stopped,
failed, held and unexecuted denominators separately. This recipe itself executed0.

