493b1f003cc8b75fd092ce0d25843f2418351dfc blob 11419
# Priority command workflows — READY / HANDOFF

Date: August 28, 2026. **Preparation ready for independent review; runtime GO is HOLD.**
This different leaf authored no implementation and ran no product, comparator,
native oracle, compiler, build, install, network or private engine. Nothing here
certifies a runtime pass, parity, superiority, release, 72-hour duration or live HEAD.

## Binding and ownership

Only this new directory is owned. It was absent at initial inspection; the index
was empty. Foreign untracked artifacts, old evidence and all production files are
preserved. Exact priority authority is docs/COMMAND_PRIORITIES.md at

dcaa5ccc54fb31b48d16a207484ea15a3bbedc91.

Selected composition: **8437e4eda904e1248c25eeef0d9d455b1d251495**.
Accepted independent evidence: **633f6c82f738f1c69d6c7b6c91672524ec8688b2**.
Full858 package SHA256: **6b5863d51ecd6484b79b7141a2004c04b775f9894d5b80bb016a02ffbefed40e**.
BINDINGS.json names exact receipts, selected revisions/blobs/SHA256, six inspected
public declarations, tool inventories and archive pointers. The selected tree is
derived, not a commit or necessarily a stored Git object; do not substitute HEAD.
No c0ada arrays, XAN, YQ or other live overlay is admitted. No jq/engine behavior
or source bodies were inspected. Metadata referring to such components is not a
behavioral review. The whole archive was bounded-decoded only to reach receipt and
package declaration data; no source string was decoded as code or evaluated.
Source closure is referenced, not copied. Selected relevant blobs were read as data;
uninspected closure and historic tool qualification remain explicitly inherited.

## Packet and denominator

CASES.json fixes **24 workflow identities plus 7 separate controls**, all unexecuted.
FIXTURES.json contains byte data and declarative infrastructure, not command handlers.
Twenty-two workflows contain both sed and rg as top-level commands; P16 additionally
combines sed with genuine find-dispatched rg. P17 deliberately keeps NUL path records
out of line-oriented transformations. This is engineering weighting toward the
user's sed332184/rg147000 counts, not a measured flag-frequency distribution.

| ID | Practical coverage / distinguishing obligation |
| --- | --- |
| P01 | Number actionable rows within a release-note slice |
| P02 | Isolate one deployment block before error search |
| P03 | Reformat key/value captures before fixed-string review |
| P04 | Replace repeated placeholders after the first occurrence |
| P05 | Extract case-insensitive substitutions without duplicate auto-print |
| P06 | Apply ordered inline and VFS programs to a config report |
| P07 | Edit a spaced filename with a byte-exact backup |
| P08 | Compare first records across separate input files |
| P09 | Join paired records before identifying an actionable pair |
| P10 | Remove debug noise while preserving search context |
| P11 | Retain UTF-8 while changing an ASCII prefix |
| P12 | Inspect the final unterminated record |
| P13 | Format argument pairs into searchable fixed-width rows |
| P14 | Audit hidden TypeScript files while excluding generated matches |
| P15 | Persist a full listing and number filtered discovery paths |
| P16 | Discover spaced paths and dispatch a literal search per file |
| P17 | Return NUL-delimited matches for option-looking and unusual paths |
| P18 | Read search patterns from stdin while searching a named file |
| P19 | Keep an empty search stream empty despite a matching cwd file |
| P20 | Prefer explicit file argv over unrelated incoming stdin |
| P21 | Assemble file/stdin/file then review a bounded line window |
| P22 | Preserve NUL through byte windows and explicit text search |
| P23 | Download a mocked report into VFS and number action items |
| P24 | Upload VFS bytes, follow authorized redirect, then search response |

Other priorities appear in actual compositions: printf/echo report generation,
cat concatenation, nl independent numbering, head/tail line and byte windows,
find literal dispatch, ls persisted listing. curl is optional explicit registration
in P23/P24 and C05-C07 only; no ambient network capability is installed. git, node
and apply_patch remain requested but owned elsewhere: no stub, alias, fake command,
host-tool substitute or pretend dispatch test is included.

| Controls | Separate purpose, never counted as workflow success |
| --- | --- |
| C01 | Declared unsupported sed -z, exact diagnostic/status2/no input read |
| C02 | rg stdin pattern/data conflict; zero pulls, one Shell cursor return |
| C03 | ReadOnlyFileSystem failure; no backing publication or backup |
| C04 | Typed provider read fault; rg2 versus pipeline0, no hidden diagnostics |
| C05 | Cooperative registered acquisition cleanup; root reason object identity |
| C06 | Destination-specific stdout closure; body/header files survive, curl141 |
| C07 | Opaque nonpreemptible authorizer; late rejection observed, no false drain |

The seven controls are future product controls, not seven observed passes. The
separate eight SCHEMA.json mutations are synthetic malformed-data controls only.
No implementation mutant is created, imported or executed.

## Novelty against existing breadth23+10

The exact existing LEGACY-RECIPES.json (23) and WORKFLOWS.json (10) under
 tests/comparison/breadth-continuation-20260828/ were inspected as data and hashed
in BINDINGS.json. None of the 23 scripts dispatches sed or rg; their nl-positive
is a standalone numbering recipe, not P01/P15/P23's transformed-stream numbering.
Old W01 uses grep/cut/sort/uniq/tee; our release-block and config-edit cases exercise
sed addresses/captures/in-place flags and rg selection/formatting instead. Old W03
is timeout0 binary identity; P22 uses printf, byte slicing, explicit text-mode rg
and substitution. Old W10 is default shell glob expansion; P14/P15 exercise rg's
hidden/positive/negative globs and VFS discovery, not a renamed glob fixture.
Old W02/W04-W09 concern split/getopts/HTML/du/which/checksums/copy-move cleanup;
none substitutes for P18-P20 stdin provenance, filename NUL records, or curl
request/redirect/credential and destination-lifecycle obligations. These24 do not
rescore, replace or extend the denominator of the existing33 or historical54.

## Exactness and observation limits

Each case fixes script, literal argv, input bytes, stdout/stderr bytes, script
status, stage statuses, namespace changes/absence and independent static reasoning.
The argv list is source order, not a claim about pipeline scheduling. Compare
ShellResult.stdoutBytes/stderrBytes, not decoded strings. Thrown controls have no
ShellResult/status: compare caller reference identity and collected external sink
bytes. Do not compare reason objects by message or JSON equality. C06 is a returned
141 with a distinct EPIPE sink reason, not a thrown caller cancellation.

Future snapshots cover the entire Memory VFS root: /, /work, declared files and
ancestor directories, with no hidden HOME/tmp/bin setup. Exact final keys/types,
bytes and initial permission bits are required. New file modes/times/identities
are not asserted. Explicit absent lists supplement this whole-namespace check;
no extra transient write is excused by later deleting it. Snapshot/setup reads are
separate harness roles and must not pollute command read/write traces.

Infrastructure wrappers forward capabilities, signals, bytes and methods faithfully;
outer VFS API calls alone count as mutation events, not Memory's internal calls.
Without a per-case exactCalls guard, mutation attempts are permitted only at the
literal changedFiles paths and must have the exact final bytes; no exact call-count
claim is made there. Read guards assert only enumerated properties, not invented
universal read counts. Discovered-file ignore metadata probes are allowed; no
ambient host content or credentials are. Network rows require exact route order,
method/headers/body bytes and no extra authorizations/requests. Body absence (null)
is distinct from an empty upload. Compare auth data including absent redirectFrom;
signal/registerCleanup are separately observed capabilities, not serialized values.

Normal mock responses use finite explicit iterators: each declared chunk once,
then one done; natural exhaustion means return0. A redirected response is disposed
without constructing its body iterator. Dispose is one shared idempotent completion;
count actual underlying invocations, not repeated calls of the product's wrapper.
C05's admitted host acquisition has synchronous cleanup enrollment and a finite
release gate. C07 intentionally does not: its promise remains pending at exec
settlement, is then explicitly rejected, and must settle before harness teardown.
No control claims arbitrary host preemption, universal cleanup, constant memory,
provider transactionality, DNS confinement or RSS containment.

## Gaps and mandatory future prerequisites

- **G01 declared limitation:** selected sed.ts:357-376 rejects -z; shared.ts:95-98
  predicts status2 and literal unsupported-option diagnostic. C01 documents refusal,
  not NUL-record compatibility. Desired argv/VFS/stdin is in the early gap report.
- **G02 declared limitation:** selected search/options.ts:159 rejects rg -t/-T;
  rg.ts:159-163 predicts status2. Globs in P14 are useful, not a substitute type DB.
  The search README's host-glob warning is stale for selected glob.ts:12-31, which
  uses the worker protocol; this packet changes no other owner's documentation.
- **G03 adapter HOLD:** the accepted run-v2 runner hardcodes C/R/H schemas, helper
  names, prior-review state and witness sets. It cannot consume this packet now.
  EXECUTION-RECIPE.md defines one minimal future owned adapter path, not an executor
  implementation or permission to launch the old runner wholesale.
- **G04 worker-observation HOLD:** regex client.ts:79-83 sets Worker execArgv:[];
  accepted210 parent-load records have no worker entry. Reuse parent loader/guard,
  but require finite worker admission and cleanup receipts before runtime GO.
  Do not infer worker coverage from214 declarations,858 files or210 parent modules.

G01/G02 are source-declared limitations, not newly executed failures or full GNU
incompatibility findings. No suspected product defect has been established.
Early report: /tmp/priority-command-workflows-prep-20260828-gap.txt.

A different review must approve literal expectations, infrastructure controls,
worker admission and the future adapter before a separately recorded root GO.
GO must name this packet's committed bytes, exact tools/source/package, three
layouts, finite cases/controls, owned capture path and remaining parent budget.
No automatic GO follows from metadata validation. Follow EXECUTION-RECIPE.md;
never repair expectations from observed output, widen imports, raise timeouts,
retry failed subjects or turn missing prerequisites into passes.

## Preparation-only check

Run only: node tests/integration/priority-command-workflows-20260828/verify.mjs

This builtin-only checker reads this packet, checks hashes/counts/schema/byte
encodings and rejects eight in-memory malformed-data variants. It never evaluates
scripts, imports virtual-bash, starts subprocesses, reads live production or rewrites
evidence. Its success means data consistency only. MANIFEST.json binds every
other packet file; the explicit-path commit binds the manifest itself.

